// NO shadowing (E0055): one name, one meaning, per scope stack. A binder — here a function
// parameter — may not reuse a name already bound in a visible scope (`base` is a top-level
// binding the function body could read). Assignment never re-declares (it reassigns, under
// E0006/E0007), and `is`-narrowing refines the same binding, so shadowing is never needed.
// expect: error E0055 at 7:6
// expect: exit 1
base = 100;
fn f(base: int): int { return base; }
echo f(5);
echo base;
